    <string name="about_title">About NephroCare</string>
    <string name="about_text">NephroCare is a companion app for people with kidney failure and on dialysis: health education, personal follow-up of weight, blood pressure, tests, fluids and medicines, reminders, and a PDF summary for the doctor. It works offline and keeps your data on the phone.</string>
    <string name="about_safety_title">Medical safety</string>
    <string name="about_review_title">Medical review</string>
    <string name="about_review_text">The first version of the educational content was written from widely accepted patient-education sources (KDIGO, national kidney foundations, dialysis nursing guides). It must be reviewed and adapted by a nephrologist before clinical use. Reference values are indicative only.</string>
    <string name="about_sources_title">Sources and licences</string>
    <string name="about_sources_text">Quran text and translations of meanings: Noble Quran Encyclopedia via quran-json (CC BY-SA 4.0). Food values: approximations from public food composition tables (USDA FoodData Central, Ciqual). Prayer times: astronomical calculation on the phone.</string>
    <string name="privacy_title">Privacy</string>
    <string name="privacy_text">• Your data is stored only on this phone, in the app\'s private storage. NephroCare has no account, no server, no advertising and no analytics.\n• Nothing is shared without your action: reports and backups leave the phone only when you send or save them yourself.\n• Android cloud backup is disabled for this app so health data is not copied to the cloud without you. Use the encrypted backup (AES-256, protected by your password) to move your data.\n• Notifications on the lock screen never show health details; medicine names are hidden unless you allow them.\n• You can lock the app with a PIN, which also blocks screenshots.\n• You can delete all your data at any time in Settings.\n• Internet is only used to play a web video you added yourself.</string>
